---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../config/site'
import '../styles/doc.css'
---

<!-- Player-facing summary of Terms Section 14 (Fair Play and Prohibited
     Conduct) and Section 20 (Suspension and Termination). The Terms govern;
     this page must never contradict them. -->
<LegalLayout
  title={`Community Rules — ${site.name}`}
  description={`What gets an account suspended in ${site.name}, how to report a player, and what happens after a report.`}
  canonical={`${site.url}/community-rules`}
>
  <h1>Community Rules</h1>
  <p class="doc-meta">
    Short version: play your best, leave the table as you found it, and do not
    try to move chips between accounts. The binding version is in our
    <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Play the game properly</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Play your own moves. No bots, scripts, modified clients, or automation
      of any kind.</li>
    <li>Do not stall. Letting the clock run to annoy an opponent is a
      forfeitable offence.</li>
    <li>Do not quit a losing match to dodge the result. Finished or abandoned,
      the match is scored.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>One person, one account</h2>
  <p>
    Extra accounts used to feed chips to a main account, to reach easier
    opponents, or to farm rewards are the most common form of cheating in a
    game like this. Accounts found doing it lose their balances and are closed
    — all of them.
  </p>

  <h2>Do not attack the game itself</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No exploiting bugs. If you find one, report it; we would rather thank
      you than ban you.</li>
    <li>No tampering with the app, the network traffic, or our servers.</li>
    <li>No buying, selling, or trading accounts, Coins, or Gems anywhere.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Respect the person on the other side</h2>
  <p>
    Display names are public. Names that are hateful, sexual, threatening,
    impersonate someone, or advertise something else will be reset or the
    account closed.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting someone</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with
    your display name, your opponent's display name, roughly when the match
    happened, and a screenshot if you have one. Every match is recorded, so we
    can review what actually took place.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens after a report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We review the recorded match and the account history behind it.</li>
    <li>Depending on what we find: a warning, removal of chips gained unfairly,
      a temporary suspension, or a permanent closure.</li>
    <li>We do not report back on another player's punishment — that is their
      private account information.</li>
    <li>If your own account is actioned and you think we got it wrong, reply to
      us. A person will look again.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Appeals and closures</h2>
  <p>
    Suspension and termination are covered by our <a href="/terms">Terms</a>,
    Section 20. Coins and Gems held by a closed account are forfeited and have
    no cash value, as set out in Sections 6 and 8.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
